          "key": "B",
          "text": "Run on two Availability Zones in one AWS Region, using another AWS Region for the disaster recovery site."
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "text": "Run on two Availability Zones in one AWS Region, using a local AWS Region for the disaster recovery site."
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "Run across two AWS Regions, using a third AWS Region for the disaster recovery site."
        }
      ],
      "correct": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation": "For high availability plus recovery from a regional service interruption, run across two Availability Zones in one Region and use a DIFFERENT AWS Region as the disaster-recovery site. Keeping the DR site in the same Region wouldn't survive a regional outage, and running active across multiple Regions is more than this requirement asks.",
